        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A refurbished treadmill is worth it when the seller can show you two
            things:</strong> a written, in-home warranty and a list of what was replaced. With
            those, it is often the best value in the market; without them, it is a
            <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">used treadmill</a>
            at a higher price.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Compare against a new machine on sale rather than list price, inspect it on delivery, and
            use it properly during the warranty so any fault surfaces while it is still covered.
          </p>
